# The Humanist and the Library: Promoting New Scholarship through Collaborative Interaction between Humanists and Librarians.

**Authors:** Burnette, Michaelyn, And Others

## Abstract
Discusses the research methodologies of humanities scholars and describes a project developed at the University of California at Berkeley that promoted collaboration between reference librarians and humanities faculty to increase faculty awareness of library services and resources. Highlights include new technologies and librarians' integration into the scholarly research process. (10 references) (LRW)

